WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:04.580
From original cast members to newcomers like
Callie Haverda and Reyn Doi, here's where

00:00:04.580 --> 00:00:07.018
you've seen these "That '90s Show" stars before.

00:00:07.220 --> 00:00:10.520
Kurtwood Smith is back as Eric's no-nonsense
father, Red Forman.

00:00:10.520 --> 00:00:13.750
However, this time he'll be laying down the
law with his granddaughter Leia.

00:00:13.750 --> 00:00:17.830
In an exclusive interview with Looper, Smith
expressed his excitement at returning to the

00:00:17.830 --> 00:00:22.929
franchise and noted that he and his on-screen
wife Debra Jo Rupp easily fell back into step on set.

00:00:22.929 --> 00:00:27.449
Since Red and Kitty agreed to stay in Point
Place in the finale of "That '70s Show," viewers

00:00:27.449 --> 00:00:30.759
were finally able to catch up on what these
characters have been up to between 1980 and

00:00:30.759 --> 00:00:34.280
1995 in season one of "That 90s Show."

00:00:34.280 --> 00:00:39.041
During the 16-year interim, Smith has added
a number of film and TV credits to his varied filmography.

00:00:39.041 --> 00:00:43.420
Notably, the actor has starred in the second
season of Marvel's "Agent Carter" as Vernon

00:00:43.420 --> 00:00:45.969
Masters, a role that was written with him
in mind.

00:00:45.969 --> 00:00:50.180
He then went on to guest star in a handful
of popular series like "Suits" and "Jupiter's

00:00:50.180 --> 00:00:54.070
Legacy," before having a role on the Hulu
mini series, "The Dropout." Smith plays David

00:00:54.070 --> 00:00:59.840
Boies in the Amanda Seyfried-led biographical crime drama, which was nominated for six Primetime Emmy Awards.

00:00:59.840 --> 00:01:04.110
Fans of "That '70s Show" might have also noticed
him playing Old Man Peterson in "The Ranch,"

00:01:04.110 --> 00:01:07.125
another Netflix comedy led by co-star Ashton
Kutcher.

00:01:07.125 --> 00:01:11.430
Joining Red for the difficult task of keeping
Leia in line is his wife, Kitty.

00:01:11.430 --> 00:01:15.640
Debra Jo Rupp reprises her role as the fan-favorite
character who is best known for being something

00:01:15.640 --> 00:01:18.300
of a mother figure to all of Eric's friends.

00:01:18.300 --> 00:01:22.240
Rupp continued to work on family-orientated
shows when "That '70s Show" wrapped, taking

00:01:22.240 --> 00:01:26.009
roles in shows like "Better with You," "This
Is Us," and "I Feel Bad."

00:01:26.009 --> 00:01:30.549
Rupp's extensive TV credits also include guest
stints on other popular series like "Hart

00:01:30.549 --> 00:01:32.579
of Dixie" and "Grey's Anatomy."

00:01:32.579 --> 00:01:36.670
In 2021, she joined the Marvel Cinematic Universe
as a series regular in "WandaVision," the

00:01:36.670 --> 00:01:38.790
first installment of Marvel's Phase 4.

00:01:38.790 --> 00:01:44.750
"That '90s Show" viewers might recognize Rupp
in her role as Westview Citizen Sharon Davis, aka.

00:01:44.750 --> 00:01:45.750
Mrs. Hart.

00:01:45.750 --> 00:01:48.920
Speaking about her role in the miniseries,
Rupp told Looper in an exclusive interview

00:01:48.920 --> 00:01:52.280
that her sitcom and theater background is
really what sealed the deal on her getting

00:01:52.280 --> 00:01:53.280
the part.

00:01:53.280 --> 00:01:56.659
Although she was initially hesitant, Rupp
loved being a part of "WandaVision," saying:

00:02:11.690 --> 00:02:14.273
"We had such a lovely time."

00:02:14.273 --> 00:02:18.430
The first and most important addition to the
new cast of "That '90s Show" is Callie Haverda,

00:02:18.430 --> 00:02:21.209
who takes on the role of Eric and Donna's
teenage daughter, Leia.

00:02:21.209 --> 00:02:24.709
Texas native Haverda has been acting since
she was six years old, telling her high school

00:02:24.709 --> 00:02:27.310
paper The Westwood Horizon in a 2022 interview,

00:02:38.569 --> 00:02:43.675
Haverda is best known for her role as Lala
Marks in the Hulu crime drama "Shut Eye" in 2017.

00:02:43.675 --> 00:02:47.430
"That '90s Show" is undoubtedly Haverda's
biggest role to date, though, and a defining

00:02:47.430 --> 00:02:48.830
moment in the actor's career.

00:02:48.830 --> 00:02:53.069
She told The Horizon that her career previously
lacked direction, and finding Leia's character

00:02:53.069 --> 00:02:57.575
sparked something in her, saying,

00:02:57.775 --> 00:03:01.790
"That '90s Show" is all about Leia connecting
with her own group of friends, beginning with

00:03:01.790 --> 00:03:04.360
the rebellious Riot grrrl, Gwen.

00:03:04.360 --> 00:03:08.670
Played by Ashley Aufderheide, Gwen is Leia's
next-door neighbor, and the two hit it off immediately.

00:03:08.670 --> 00:03:13.310
In fact, Gwen literally lives in Donna's old
house, since Bob Pinciotti moved to Florida

00:03:13.310 --> 00:03:15.150
at the beginning of the '80s.

00:03:15.150 --> 00:03:20.827
"You found the people who don't fit in, and
I am their queen."

00:03:20.827 --> 00:03:25.629
Prior to joining the cast, Aufderheide's biggest
roles included ABC's sci-fi mystery-drama

00:03:25.629 --> 00:03:30.019
"Emergence" an indie flick "Infinitely Polar
Bear," which stars Mark Ruffalo and Zoe Saldana.

00:03:30.019 --> 00:03:33.870
In 2020, she also featured in the British
fantasy film "Four Kids and It."

00:03:34.117 --> 00:03:37.550
Gwen isn't the only next-door neighbor Leia
gets to know.

00:03:37.550 --> 00:03:41.500
She soon befriends Gwen's fun-loving brother
Nate, who is played by Maxwell Acee Donovan.

00:03:41.500 --> 00:03:45.569
Nate and Gwen have an interesting dynamic
on the show, and somewhat replicates Eric

00:03:45.569 --> 00:03:48.800
and Laurie's relationship since Leia is an
only child.

00:03:48.800 --> 00:03:52.000
Viewers might know the actor behind Nate's
big smile from his starring role in the Disney

00:03:52.000 --> 00:03:54.890
Channel series, "Gabby Duran &amp; The Unsittables."

00:03:54.890 --> 00:03:58.739
Donovan plays the titular character Gabby's
best friend Wesley Presley and he credits

00:03:58.739 --> 00:04:02.230
the comedy series for making his dream of
an acting career a reality.

00:04:02.230 --> 00:04:06.200
Prior to bagging this longstanding main role,
Donovan had some smaller supporting roles,

00:04:06.200 --> 00:04:10.319
such as the TV miniseries "Greenlit," and
the Zoey Deutch and Nicholas Braun-led rom-com,

00:04:10.319 --> 00:04:11.319
"Good Kids."

00:04:11.634 --> 00:04:17.019
Newcomer Sam Morelos stars in "That '90s Show"
as the ambitious and intelligent teenager Nikki.

00:04:17.019 --> 00:04:19.350
There's a lot more than meets the eye when
it comes to Nikki.

00:04:19.350 --> 00:04:23.250
Deadline described her, as having, quote,
"more rebellion than a frustrated debutante,

00:04:23.250 --> 00:04:26.280
and her boyfriend Nate can scratch that itch."

00:04:26.280 --> 00:04:30.660
Nikki is Morelos' first TV role, but she's
previously starred in a couple of short films,

00:04:30.660 --> 00:04:33.120
including "Forgetting Nobody" and "Extraordinary
Night."

00:04:33.120 --> 00:04:37.320
When filming Season 1 of "That '90s Show"
concluded, Morelos took to Instagram to celebrate

00:04:37.320 --> 00:04:40.060
the experience and everything leading up to
it.

00:04:40.060 --> 00:04:42.072
Alongside some behind-the-scenes content,
she wrote:

00:04:49.543 --> 00:04:54.440
Mace Coronel plays the flirty aspiring videographer
Jay, another member of Leia's gang, as well

00:04:54.440 --> 00:04:57.300
as her love interest.

00:04:57.300 --> 00:04:59.809
"Hey girl."

00:04:59.809 --> 00:05:03.420
With more than a decade of acting experience
behind him, "That '90s Show" viewers will

00:05:03.420 --> 00:05:05.380
likely have seen Coronel before.

00:05:05.380 --> 00:05:06.520
He got his start playing R.J.

00:05:06.520 --> 00:05:12.560
Forrester in "The Bold and the Beautiful,"
before starring in the 2014 TV movie, "Santa Hunters."

00:05:12.560 --> 00:05:16.190
However, Coronel is probably best known for
starring in Nickelodeon's comedy series "Nicky,

00:05:16.190 --> 00:05:17.470
Ricky, Dicky &amp; Dawn."

00:05:17.470 --> 00:05:21.280
He played Dicky, one of the titular quadruplets
of the Harper family, but he left abruptly

00:05:21.280 --> 00:05:23.280
in the middle of production on the fourth
season.

00:05:23.280 --> 00:05:26.981
He announced his departure in a since-deleted
Instagram post, which explained that it was

00:05:26.981 --> 00:05:30.220
a mutual decision so he could focus on other
roles.

00:05:30.220 --> 00:05:34.900
As promised, Coronel diversified his filmography,
and he went on to star in short films and

00:05:34.900 --> 00:05:35.900
some miniseries.

00:05:35.900 --> 00:05:39.900
He said on his Instagram that he hoped the
2019 short film "Pocket," which is a commentary

00:05:39.900 --> 00:05:44.300
on social media and having the world in your
pocket, would be an "eye-opening” film for audiences.

00:05:44.300 --> 00:05:48.820
He followed this up with roles in "Wireless"
and Colin Kaepernick and Ava DuVernay's drama

00:05:48.820 --> 00:05:50.050
"Colin in Black and White."

00:05:50.525 --> 00:05:55.070
As beloved as "That '70s Show" is, parts of
it wouldn't be accepted today and that includes

00:05:55.070 --> 00:05:57.990
its lack of LGBTQ characters and storylines.

00:05:57.990 --> 00:06:02.470
While the short-lived spinoff "That '80s Show"
had a bisexual character, Reyn Doi will play

00:06:02.470 --> 00:06:05.490
the TV franchise's first openly gay character,
Ozzie.

00:06:05.490 --> 00:06:10.620
Doi has been acting since 2017, bagging his
first job as a dancer in a Sonos commercial.

00:06:10.620 --> 00:06:14.650
He quickly racked up a number of credits in
commercials and short films, before playing

00:06:14.650 --> 00:06:18.639
Takeshi, the son of an extradited fugitive,
in an episode of the crime-action series "S.W.A.T."

00:06:18.639 --> 00:06:19.639
in 2020.

00:06:19.639 --> 00:06:23.441
His big breakout role came the following year,
though, when he played Yoyo in "Barb and Star

00:06:23.441 --> 00:06:24.800
Go to Vista Del Mar."

00:06:24.800 --> 00:06:29.650
He plays Kristen Wiig's sidekick, but as the
New York Post notes, Doi quickly steals the show.

00:06:29.650 --> 00:06:34.199
At the same time, Doi was working on the Nickelodeon
family comedy "Side Hustle," and the TV movie

00:06:34.199 --> 00:06:35.104
"Adopted."

00:06:35.104 --> 00:06:39.550
Actor and musician Olivia Sanabia has a supporting
role in "That '90s Show" as Serena.

00:06:39.550 --> 00:06:44.180
She is best known for starring in the Amazon
Studios series "Just Add Magic" from 2016

00:06:44.180 --> 00:06:49.400
to 2019, in which she plays Kelly Quinn in
51 of the show's 52 episodes.

00:06:49.400 --> 00:06:53.180
While filming the third season of the magical
dramedy, Sanabia started working on the Disney

00:06:53.180 --> 00:06:55.590
Channel series "Coop &amp; Cami Ask the World."

00:06:55.590 --> 00:06:59.099
When that show ended, she bagged guest roles
in a variety of other notable series.

00:06:59.099 --> 00:07:03.550
You might recognize her as Luanne in "Country
Comfort," McKenna in "This Is Us," and Hailey

00:07:03.550 --> 00:07:05.330
from "Colin in Black and White."

00:07:05.330 --> 00:07:07.479
Viewers may also know Sanabia as a singer.

00:07:07.479 --> 00:07:11.860
Her discography includes three original singles
— "Star Crossed," "Evergreen," and "The

00:07:11.860 --> 00:07:16.190
Train" — the latter of which is a particularly
important message about accepting your differences.

00:07:16.190 --> 00:07:19.180
Sanabia explained in a 2020 interview with
Girls' Life,

00:07:24.866 --> 00:07:28.680
Topher Grace was the leading man in "That
'70s Show" before he departed ahead of Season

00:07:28.680 --> 00:07:30.169
8 to star in "Spider-Man 3."

00:07:30.169 --> 00:07:34.410
He did, however, return for the series finale
and conclude his story by getting back together

00:07:34.410 --> 00:07:35.410
with Donna.

00:07:35.410 --> 00:07:39.840
Grace's early exit is one of the sore points
of "That '70s Show," and to add insult to

00:07:39.840 --> 00:07:43.938
injury, "Spider-Man 3" was largely panned,
with director Sam Raimi even calling the film awful.

00:07:43.938 --> 00:07:48.870
"I'm gonna put some dirt in your eye."

00:07:48.870 --> 00:07:52.690
It somewhat put the brakes on Grace's rising
star, but he has since gone on to enjoy big

00:07:52.690 --> 00:07:54.120
movie success.

00:07:54.120 --> 00:07:58.740
Since the 2007 superhero film, Grace has starred
in a handful of notable features like "Interstellar,"

00:07:58.740 --> 00:08:02.400
"American Ultra," "War Machine," "Delirium,"
and BlacKkKlansman.

00:08:02.400 --> 00:08:06.470
He's also found a permanent home on the TV
comedy "Home Economics" which follows Grace

00:08:06.470 --> 00:08:10.560
as Tom, the oldest of three siblings who are
all in different financial situations.

00:08:10.560 --> 00:08:14.600
Speaking of family shows, returning to the
world of Point Place again for "That '90s

00:08:14.600 --> 00:08:16.810
Show" felt like a family reunion for Grace.

00:08:16.810 --> 00:08:17.810
He told ET,

00:08:26.468 --> 00:08:30.740
"That '90s Show" had a lot of work to do to
connect the dots between the finale of "That

00:08:30.740 --> 00:08:35.399
'70s Show" and 1995, including Donna's story
of raising Leia and becoming a writer.

00:08:35.399 --> 00:08:39.520
Laura Prepon certainly believes it does her
character justice, telling Us Weekly before

00:08:39.520 --> 00:08:40.780
season 1 was released,

00:08:45.000 --> 00:08:48.840
Donna has clearly been busy over the last
decade and a half, and so has Prepon.

00:08:48.840 --> 00:08:52.310
After playing the red-haired tomboy for eight
years, Prepon took on the lead role in the

00:08:52.310 --> 00:08:54.279
NBC sitcom "Are You There, Chelsea?"

00:08:54.279 --> 00:08:58.430
Of course, "That '90s Show" viewers probably
know her best from her long stint as the dark-haired

00:08:58.430 --> 00:09:01.529
maven Alex Vause in "Orange Is the New Black."

00:09:01.529 --> 00:09:05.870
While filming the comedy-drama, Prepon also
appeared as Cathy in the 2016 psychological

00:09:05.870 --> 00:09:07.582
thriller "The Girl on the Train."

00:09:07.582 --> 00:09:11.370
With Eric and Donna coming back, why not try
to get as much of the whole gang back together

00:09:11.370 --> 00:09:12.370
as possible?

00:09:12.370 --> 00:09:16.640
Mila Kunis confirmed her return to the franchise
as Jackie Burkhart in an interview with Access

00:09:16.640 --> 00:09:20.070
Hollywood, where she explained the different
relationship dynamics which have taken place

00:09:20.070 --> 00:09:21.820
off-screen since the finale.

00:09:21.820 --> 00:09:26.130
Although Jackie and Wilmer Valderrama's character,
Fez, were together when the series ended,

00:09:26.130 --> 00:09:30.390
everyone knew she was meant to end up with
her husband Ashton Kutcher's character, Kelso.

00:09:30.390 --> 00:09:34.220
Before season 1 even came out, the actor let
slip a few details about her part in the upcoming

00:09:34.220 --> 00:09:38.450
series, including the fact that Jackie and
Kelso are now married with a kid.

00:09:38.450 --> 00:09:41.550
Since 2006, Kunis has starred in a string
of movies.

00:09:41.550 --> 00:09:45.380
She's been in romantic comedies like "Forgetting
Sarah Marshall," and "Friends With Benefits."

00:09:45.380 --> 00:09:48.960
She's been in action comedies like "The Spy
Who Dumped Me" and romantic action-adventure

00:09:48.960 --> 00:09:50.570
films like "Jupiter Ascending."

00:09:50.570 --> 00:09:54.360
She's also been in more dramatic features
like the Academy Award nominated-film, "Black

00:09:54.360 --> 00:09:57.530
Swan," and 2022's "Luckiest Girl Alive."

00:09:57.530 --> 00:10:01.450
As well as this, Kunis has voiced the character
of Meg Griffin in "Family Guy" since Season

00:10:01.450 --> 00:10:02.450
2 in 1999.

00:10:02.450 --> 00:10:06.760
"That '90s Show" is one of only a few times
she's shared the screen with Kutcher since

00:10:06.760 --> 00:10:08.050
the original series.

00:10:08.050 --> 00:10:10.000
Kunis said of returning to the show with Kutcher,

00:10:12.828 --> 00:10:17.010
Ashton Kutcher credits "That '70s Show" with
kick-starting his career and told Variety

00:10:17.010 --> 00:10:20.839
in a 2022 interview that the reason he and
his wife Mila Kunis are returning for the

00:10:20.839 --> 00:10:23.186
spinoff is so that they can pay homage to
that.

00:10:23.186 --> 00:10:23.958
He said,

00:10:27.390 --> 00:10:30.950
In the years between the original series and
"That '90s Show," Kutcher has enjoyed a very

00:10:30.950 --> 00:10:33.399
successful film and television career.

00:10:33.399 --> 00:10:36.639
Viewers will no doubt recognize him from one
of his roles in romantic comedy films such

00:10:36.639 --> 00:10:41.180
as "What Happens in Vegas," "Valentine's Day,
"Killers," and "No Strings Attached."

00:10:41.180 --> 00:10:45.700
From 2011 to 2015 Kutcher also starred in
the beloved comedy series, "Two and a Half

00:10:45.700 --> 00:10:47.890
Men," replacing lead Charlie Sheen.

00:10:47.890 --> 00:10:51.960
While speaking on the "WTF With Marc Maron"
podcast, Kutcher explains that he owes much

00:10:51.960 --> 00:10:56.230
of his comedic success to "That '70s Show"
creator Bonnie Turner, who taught him the,

00:10:56.230 --> 00:10:57.670
quote, "rhythms of comedy."

00:10:57.670 --> 00:11:03.440
From 2016 to 2020 Kutcher focused on TV, namely
his role as Colt Bennett in Netflix's family

00:11:03.440 --> 00:11:04.859
dramedy, "The Ranch."

00:11:04.859 --> 00:11:09.639
Kutcher has since returned to features, starring
in the 2022 black comedy "Vengeance" alongside

00:11:09.639 --> 00:11:13.823
B.J. Novak, Boyd Holbrook, Issa Rae, Dove Cameron,
and John Mayer.

00:11:13.823 --> 00:11:17.630
Wilmer Valderrama is best known for playing
foreign exchange student Fez in all eight

00:11:17.630 --> 00:11:19.700
seasons of "That '70s Show."

00:11:19.700 --> 00:11:23.649
Since it ended, Valderrama has been the architect
of his career, intentionally choosing varied

00:11:23.649 --> 00:11:26.139
projects in different genres to work on.

00:11:26.139 --> 00:11:30.810
Some of his notable credits include "From
Prada to Nada," "From Dusk til Dawn: The Series,"

00:11:30.810 --> 00:11:32.880
"Minority Report," and "NCIS."

00:11:32.880 --> 00:11:37.300
Speaking to People in 2022, Valderrama explained
the responsibility he felt during the early

00:11:37.300 --> 00:11:39.670
stages of his career as a Latino actor.

00:11:39.670 --> 00:11:40.670
He shared,

00:11:50.909 --> 00:11:52.910
"But I do need you to lower that weapon."

00:11:52.910 --> 00:11:55.446
"Please and thank you."

00:11:55.446 --> 00:11:59.310
Fans may also recognize Valderrama from his
recurring role in "The Ranch," in which he

00:11:59.310 --> 00:12:04.248
plays Umberto, and his five-episode guest
stint on "Grey's Anatomy" as patient Kyle Diaz.

00:12:04.248 --> 00:12:07.310
However, "That '70s Show" still holds a big
place in his heart.

00:12:07.310 --> 00:12:11.080
In fact, according to The Wall Street Journal,
Valderrama still owns the original Vista Cruiser

00:12:11.080 --> 00:12:14.100
from the series, which he purchased for $500.

00:12:14.100 --> 00:12:17.649
Although 'That 90s Show" reveals that Fez
didn't end up with Jackie because of her feelings

00:12:17.649 --> 00:12:21.750
for Keslo, things are looking up for the owner
of a successful salon chain.

00:12:21.750 --> 00:12:26.052
Hopefully his new flame, Andrea Anders' character,
Sherri, and him can make it work in the long run!

00:12:26.052 --> 00:12:30.829
"That '70s Show" alum Don Stark is also returning
for the spinoff in a supporting role as Donna's

00:12:30.829 --> 00:12:32.329
dad Bob Pinciotti.

00:12:32.329 --> 00:12:35.769
Speaking about his return to the set with
Entertainment Weekly, Stark said:

00:12:39.149 --> 00:12:42.380
All the young people who were in the new cast
were terrific, and it mirrored what it was

00:12:42.380 --> 00:12:44.010
like when we started."

00:12:44.010 --> 00:12:47.300
Viewers will of course know that Stark is
not returning with his on-screen wife, Tanya

00:12:47.300 --> 00:12:49.750
Roberts, who sadly passed away in 2021.

00:12:49.750 --> 00:12:54.800
However, his return in episode 6 of season
one is a delight, especially his karaoke performance

00:12:54.800 --> 00:12:56.800
at his granddaughter's birthday party.

00:12:56.800 --> 00:13:00.560
Since 2006, Stark has been busy guest-starring
on a variety of TV series.

00:13:00.560 --> 00:13:04.630
His knack for comedy has helped him secure
roles in the likes of "Curb Your Enthusiasm,"

00:13:04.630 --> 00:13:05.880
"Shameless" and "Dollface."

00:13:05.880 --> 00:13:10.160
He's also used his comedic acting chops to
play Jules Podell in 2018's "Green Book,"

00:13:10.160 --> 00:13:12.780
and Sol in the star-studded rom-com "Café
Society."

00:13:13.232 --> 00:13:17.699
Actor, comedian, and musician Tommy Chong
will forever be known to "That '70s Show"

00:13:17.699 --> 00:13:19.700
fans as veteran-turned-hippy stoner Leo.

00:13:19.700 --> 00:13:23.500
The beloved member of the Cheech &amp; Chong comedy
duo was an important member of the show's

00:13:23.500 --> 00:13:24.910
supporting cast.

00:13:24.910 --> 00:13:28.269
Although he wasn't present in every season,
he often showed up just in time to make some

00:13:28.269 --> 00:13:31.560
interesting observations relating to the lives
of Eric and his friends.

00:13:31.560 --> 00:13:34.830
He also took Hyde under his wing, giving him
a job at the Foto Hut.

00:13:34.830 --> 00:13:38.610
"That '90s Show" just wouldn't be complete
without an appearance from Leo, but thankfully,

00:13:38.610 --> 00:13:40.769
Chong has returned and made a fitting comeback.

00:13:40.769 --> 00:13:44.960
In fact, he hilariously doesn't seem to pick
up on many of the callbacks to "That 70s Show"

00:13:44.960 --> 00:13:47.180
or even remember Kitty and Red.

00:13:47.180 --> 00:13:51.850
Since the original series ended in 2006, Chong
has been a vocal marijuana activist.

00:13:51.850 --> 00:13:56.360
Alongside his 2006 documentary "A/k/a Tommy
Chong" which chronicles this, the actor often

00:13:56.360 --> 00:13:59.730
plays activists or characters who use drugs
freely, just like Leo.

00:13:59.730 --> 00:14:03.820
More recently, Chong played stoner Hubert
Wilson in the "Raising Hope" Season 4 episode,

00:14:03.820 --> 00:14:05.029
"The One Where They Get High."

00:14:05.029 --> 00:14:08.840
Viewers might also recognize Chong from his
appearance on "The Masked Singer" in 2019

00:14:08.840 --> 00:14:11.800
where he competed on the reality singing show
as a Pineapple.

